1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.ria1914.info/index.php?curid=17630
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Deuxième mariage, avec Malitza le 02/09/1939 à Paris.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT From the nobles of the Grand Duchy of Finland, son of Major General Mortimer Karlovich Brofeldt (09/05/1840 - 1890). Orthodox confession. General education - Pskov Cadet Corps, military - Pavlovsk Military School (1st category, 19
2 CONC 07). Released in the Life Guards Izmailovsky Regiment. From 07/18/1914 in the transport half-company of the Izmailovsky Regiment. From 01/12/1915 - in the Reserve Battalion as an adjutant. From 02/26/1916 to 03/14/1916 he was in t
2 CONC he active part of the regiment at the front, commanding the 5th company. 10/25/1916 appointed assistant to Art. Adjutant of the Directorate of the Inspector of Guard Troops. In January 1917, Assistant Art. adjutant of the Special 
2 CONC Army headquarters. Member of the White movement, died in the USA.
2 CONT Wife Olga Leonidovna Balkashina, noblewoman. Brothers Brofeldt Boris Mortimerovich and Brofeldt Vladimir Mortimerovich
