2 CONT * [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Axel_Fredrik_Londen '''Wikipedia: Axel Fredrik Londen'''] was a Finnish sports shooter, who competed in the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1912_Summer_Olympics '''Summer Olympics 1912''']
2 CONT
2 CONT * He was part of the Finnish team, which won the bronze medal in the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shooting_at_the_1912_Summer_Olympics_%E2%80%93_Men%27s_100_meter_team_running_deer,_single_shots '''100 metre running deer, single
2 CONC  shots event.'''] and finished 15th. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * As part of the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shooting_at_the_1912_Summer_Olympics_%E2%80%93_Men%27s_trap,_team '''Clay pigeons team he finished in fifth place.''']
2 CONT
2 CONT * He was a member of the board of the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Finnish_Olympic_Committee '''Finnish Olympic Committee'''] in 1907–1908 and 1911–1913.
